# Problem Definition

This tool is a vulnerability scanner that fetches cve information from several sources. 
We have some minor bugs or improvements that we need to address:

# BUG 1
In the sources tooltip with the links for the aliases, when there is more than 1 alias, the text is ok in the link but the link is always a repetition of the first link:

CVE-0000 -> link to CVE-0000
CVE-0001 -> link to CVE-0000
...
Watever -> link to CVE-0000

# BUG 2
Cancel is not cancelling. If in the middle of the scan we press cancel it doesn't stop, continues until it finishes and that is not cancel
Cancel should cancell all inflight operations and clear scans.

# BUG 3
If we have several repositories, and just select fixes for repository 1 and then commit.
If next without scanning we deselect the fixes from repository 1 and add to repository 2 and fix, when we commit it will try to commit again to repository 1

When we fix some library it should be marked as fixed as it is now but unselected and grayed out, we cannot fix what is already fixed.
When we fix some library it should be removed from statistics right away without needing additional scan
When we fix and commit on one repository it should not be marked dirty to commit again

# Feature 1

When we select a folder it will assume that the node projects are the sub-folders, we need to make this more dynamic:
1) if user selects the root and already has package.json , it should use the root folder as a project
2) there might be subdirectories inside the repository folders that have package.json, the app should search recursively
3) if there is a folder child to a already found project , ex: my_proj that has a package.json that has a subfolder called demo with a package.json, the name considered should be 'my_proj/demo'

In summary, the app should consider that there might have package.json in the selected folder or in any recursively child folder.

# Feature 2
NVD scanner sometimes have url links, if there is any link for a github advisory, enrich the information using that link that probably has also infromation about vulnerable ranges and patched versions.
So if NVD references github advisory , enrich with github advisory as well.

